          "source_quote": "ὑπὸ δὲ τῆς συνεχείας τοῦ πνεύματος χυθῆναι μὴ δυνάμενον εἰς αἵματος φύσιν μετατρέπειν ἔφασκεν τὸν ἐν αὐτῷ ἀέρα",
          "english_quote": "Next, he said, it changes the air within it—which cannot be poured out because of the spirit’s cohesion—into the nature of blood",
          "issue": "The main rendering is defensible, but the notes do not disclose a material alternative involving both agency and reference. χυθῆναι μὴ δυνάμενον can be understood as neuter, referring to the previously mentioned water as the subject of μετατρέπειν; αὐτῷ can then refer to that water. On this reading, the water cannot flow out because of the spirit’s cohesion and changes the air within itself into blood. Merely mentioning an impersonal alternative does not preserve this reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Expand the note to preserve the water-subject reading explicitly. Explain that the main text instead continues the spirit as agent, attaches χυθῆναι μὴ δυνάμενον to the air, and takes αὐτῷ as referring to the spirit, favoring continuity with the preceding spirit-agent construction. This is interpretive ambiguity, not demonstrated source corruption; no emendation or additional print verification is required. Submit the amended note and main text for fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
