          "english_quote": "You cannot be a god. Fear the God who truly is.",
          "issue": "ὄντως qualifies θεόν: the contrast is between Simon’s inability to be a god and the one who really is God. The draft’s bare “who truly is” leaves the predicate unstated and readily sounds like an existential formulation. “The real God” represents the supplied wording more clearly and preserves the immediate contrast without that additional ambiguity.",
